		<TD COLSPAN="5" BACKGROUND="images2004/GPContentBox_07.gif" valign="top">


		<b>6/11/2004 1:28:00 PM
			Theme Submissions</b>
		<p>
		Hey folks!  If you've got a great-looking site with appealing colors, custom HTML, custom CSS or other elements that you think other admins might like to import (credit to the author given, of course), you can now submit your site's style settings as a Theme!<br><br>In the Control Panel, click on "Styles &amp; Colors," then click on "Submit Theme!"
		</p>
	
		<br>
	
		<b>6/10/2004 1:36:00 PM
			Custom Welcome Messages</b>
		<p>
		You can now configure custom welcome messages for all of the different security levels.  Existing welcome messages are the "default," and you can add custom ones either by going to your control panel and modifying the content, or by clicking on the pencil icon underneath a welcome message content type you already have on your pages.
		</p>
	
		<br>
	
		<b>6/10/2004 9:20:00 AM
			Idle Monitor Enhancement</b>
		<p>
		The Idle Monitor now has a link called "Manage Exemptions," which allows the selection of members of the guild to be exempt from Idle Monitor processing.  Members marked as Exempt will not receive warnings and will not be auto-disbanded (if these options are enabled in the Idle Monitor to begin with).  This ensures that people who have given away-time notice that is approved by guild leaders are not hassled by the site.  <br><br>Note that members with Officer or higher level access, and members that have not yet been approved as members, will never be processed by the Idle Monitor, so it is not necessary to add them to the exemption list.  <br><br>A section has been added to the <a href="/FAQ.aspx?FAQEntry=52" target="_blank">Frequently Asked Questions</a> that gives an overview on the Idle Monitor and the Exemptions.
		</p>
	
		<br>
	
		<b>6/8/2004 5:20:00 AM
			Idle Monitor Live</b>
		<p>
		We've added new functionality to the Control Panel called the "Idle Monitor."  You get to it by clicking on "Site Members" and then "Idle Monitor" from the Task list.  Many thanks to the individual who recommended this at the most recent Fan Faire GuildPortal attended!<br /><br />Using this tool, SuperAdmins can have the system automatically send out customized warning e-mails to members who have been inactive for a configurable number of days.  Additionally, you can also tell the system to automatically disband anybody who has not been on for a configurable number of days, also sending an e-mail (perhaps with instructions on re-joining).<br /><br />The process that manages warning e-mails and auto-disbanding runs every other night, and will send a summary message to all appropriate admins, listing all actions that it took during a given run.
		</p>
	
		<br>
	
		<b>6/7/2004 1:18:00 AM
			Some Updates</b>
		<p>
		Hello all!  We've updated the <a href="FAQ.aspx">Frequently Asked Questions</a> page with some more information on character management, subscriptions, administration, and some general information on GuildPortal.  Also, there was a bug where guild bans on individuals by user name wouldn't always take hold (currently bans work on both user name and IP address -- though the IP is hidden to protect privacy), and code has been pushed to fix it.
		</p>
	
